    "job_description": "Turbo M.Tech | Datamind FY27\nWipro is hiring M.Tech graduates under the DAAI practice for the role of Project Engineer. The role involves working on AI-driven solutions, Python-based applications, and advanced analytics use cases. Candidates will undergo a structured and AI-enabled evaluation process, including DataMind assessment, to ensure role fitment and technical readiness.\nRequired Skills & Qualifications\nStrong knowledge of Python programming with understanding of AI and ML fundamentals.\nGood analytical and problem-solving skills with knowledge of data structures and algorithms.\nAbility to work on data-driven applications and AI-based solutions.\nEffective communication skills with the ability to collaborate in team environments.\nKey Responsibilities\nDevelop and implement AI and Python-based solutions aligned to business requirements.\nParticipate in structured evaluation processes including DataMind assessment.\nAnalyze problems and deliver scalable and efficient technical solutions.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams while adhering to defined processes and quality standards.\nEligibility criteria\nEducation\n10th Standard: 60% or above\n12th Standard: 60% or above\nGraduation and Post Graduation: 60% or CGPA Equivalent to 6.0 or above as applicable by the university guidelines\nDiploma (10+2 or 10+3): 60% or above (for candidates entering B.Tech via lateral entry)\nOther criteria\nNo active backlogs are allowed.\nMax 3 years of GAP in education allowed (between 10th to commencement Post graduation)\nNo Gaps are allowed in the Graduation period. Graduation should be completed within 4 years from the start of the Graduation.\nNo Gaps are allowed in the Post Graduation period. Post Graduation should be completed within 2 years from the start of the Post Graduation.\nLateral Entry through Diploma or B.Sc into B.Tech or BE course is eligible. Diploma course duration of 3.5 or 4 years is eligible.\nCandidates will be reinvited for the test process, who have completed 3 months of cool-off period from the previous assessment date\nShould be an Indian Citizen or should hold a PIO or OCI card, in the event of holding a passport of any other country.\nBhutan and Nepal Nationals need to submit their citizenship certificate.\nCandidates should be 18+ while registration.\nYear of passing\n2026\nQualification\nM.E / M.Tech\nBranch of study\nCS, IT, AI and related.\nDesignation\nProject Engineer\nCompensation \nINR 6.5 Lakh per annum\nBonus: 1 Lakh Retention Bonus payable upon completion of 12 months from the date of joining and merged to CTC after 1 year from the bonus payout date.\nService agreement\nApplicable for a 12month Training Agreement of INR 75,000; in case of early exit before completion of the agreement period, the candidate shall be liable to pay the applicable prorata amount to the Company.\nSelection process\n1st Round - Online Assessment\n2nd Round - Voice Assessment\n3rd Round Datamind Assessment\n4th Round - Business Discussion \nTerms and Conditions:\nIt is Wipros discretion to permit/limit the participation of each candidate in the Turbo M.Tech | Datamind FY27 recruitment process.\nThis is to formally notify you that, during the processing of your application, or at any time subsequent to your joining, should it be discovered that any information furnished by you in your application does not satisfy any of the conditions stipulated in the eligibility criteria, the Company reserves the unequivocal right to revoke/hold/terminate your candidature or employment forthwith, without notice or compensation. Additionally, the Company retains the sole discretion to initiate any action it deems appropriate in accordance with its organisational policies and all applicable laws and regulations.\nThe determination of registration parameters and the conduct of the selection procedure are exclusively at the discretion of Wipro. Wipro is under no obligation to disclose any information at any stage of the selection process. Wipro further reserves the right to issue a provisional offer to a candidate, which may be revoked should the candidate fail to satisfy any conditions precedent to employment. Moreover, Wipro reserves the right to hold the candidate liable for any involvement in unlawful activities, including but not limited to impersonation, fraud, or the submission of forged or fraudulent documents, and to pursue all remedies available under law.\nUpon successful completion of the online assessment, candidates shall be required to participate in an English communication assessment. Candidates who successfully clear the English communication assessment shall proceed to Datamind assessment. Candidates who successfully clear Datamind assessment shall be eligible for the business discussion round. Those who are successful in the business discussion round will be issued a Letter of Intent (LOI). Acceptance of the LOI by the candidate will be followed by a mandatory Background Verification (BGV) process. Issuance of the final offer letter* shall be contingent upon the candidates successful completion of the document verification and BGV processes, subject to the Companys prevailing policies and applicable laws.\n*If the candidate is required to undergo pre-skilling training, the offer letter will be issued only to those candidates who successfully clear the pre-skilling training.\nWipro will inform candidates about the results of the recruitment by individual e-mails or other means of communication provided by individual candidates. Please note that at any stage, whether during your online test, interview process, and/or during internal training or upon joining the Company, if it is brought to our notice that you have indulged in malpractices or used illegal means to clear your online assessment, the Company shall withdraw or revoke the offer with immediate effect and we reserve our rights to take suitable action against you as we may deem fit.\nShow Less"